WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.247
Teacher midterm practice for C plus plus, question 1.

2
00:00:04.867 --> 00:00:07.284
Trace this program with the table method.

3
00:00:07.284 --> 00:00:09.197
What ends up in the output box?

4
00:00:10.897 --> 00:00:13.690
Set up the table: one column per variable.

5
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.062
a starts at one, b at two, and i and sum at zero.

6
00:00:17.682 --> 00:00:23.027
Pass one. sum plus equals B of zero: eleven. Is i greater than two? No.

7
00:00:23.027 --> 00:00:26.607
a plus equals B of one, which is seven, so a is eight.

8
00:00:26.607 --> 00:00:29.772
i becomes one, and the cout prints one, eight.

9
00:00:30.391 --> 00:00:34.843
Pass two: sum is eighteen, a is fourteen, i is two. Print two, fourteen.

10
00:00:35.464 --> 00:00:40.266
Pass three: sum is twenty four, a is nineteen, i is three. Print three, nineteen.

11
00:00:40.885 --> 00:00:42.613
Pass four is the trap.

12
00:00:42.613 --> 00:00:47.200
sum plus equals B of three runs first, so sum becomes twenty nine.

13
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.941
Only then is i greater than two, and break

14
00:00:49.941 --> 00:00:53.337
exits, before a, i or the cout can change.

15
00:00:53.957 --> 00:00:59.462
After the loop, b equals sum minus i: twenty nine minus three, which is twenty six.

16
00:00:59.462 --> 00:01:03.240
The last line prints twenty nine, nineteen, twenty six.

17
00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:08.497
The theory. while of one is an infinite loop: the condition

18
00:01:08.497 --> 00:01:12.676
is always true, so only a break can end it. And order matters.

19
00:01:12.676 --> 00:01:15.236
On the final pass, every line above the break

20
00:01:15.236 --> 00:01:18.266
still runs, and every line below it is skipped.

21
00:01:19.866 --> 00:01:24.409
So the output box shows one, eight. Two, fourteen. Three, nineteen.

22
00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:27.044
And then twenty nine, nineteen, twenty six.

23
00:01:27.863 --> 00:01:31.547
The classic mistake is stopping the trace at the break test, and

24
00:01:31.547 --> 00:01:35.069
forgetting that sum was already updated on that last pass.

25
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.907
Exam tip: add a new table row whenever a variable changes, and

26
00:01:39.907 --> 00:01:43.495
copy each cout into the output box the moment it runs.

27
00:01:43.495 --> 00:01:48.494
Each print here starts with a newline, so every pair goes on its own line.
